  <h2 id="operator">1. Operator and these terms</h2>
  <p>1.1 Artur Witkowski, a sole trader entered in the Polish Central Register and Information on Business Activity (CEIDG), ul. Stefana Batorego 23/7, 81-365 Gdynia, Poland, NIP 5862405430, REGON 528542614 ("we", "us"), makes and runs Midnight Pantry. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@arturwitkowski.com">contact@arturwitkowski.com</a>, in English or Polish.</p>
  <p>1.2 These terms are the terms of service for services provided by electronic means (regulamin) required by article 8 of the Polish Act of 18 July 2002 on providing services by electronic means.</p>
  <p>1.3 These terms are available free of charge at arturwitkowski.com/midnight-pantry/terms/. You can save or print them from your browser at any time.</p>
  <p>1.4 These terms exist in English and Polish. Both versions have equal force.</p>

  <h2 id="game">2. The game</h2>
  <p>2.1 Midnight Pantry is a game for iPhone and Android. You need an iPhone with iOS 17 or later, or a phone with Android 7.0 or later. The game shows no ads.</p>
  <p>2.2 The game plays offline, without an account. An internet connection and an account are needed only for the daily contest and to keep your progress with the account.</p>
  <p>2.3 With an account you can enter the daily contest and keep your progress on our server, so it follows you to another phone. In the daily contest every player gets the same game that day, and your first try goes on the leaderboard under your nickname.</p>

  <h2 id="full-version">3. The full version</h2>
  <p>3.1 Part of the game is free. The full version is a single in-app purchase that unlocks the rest of the game. The purchase screen in the game and the store show what it includes and its price before you pay. It has no renewals and no end date.</p>
  <p>3.2 Apple sells the full version to you through the App Store, or Google through Google Play, and takes the payment. Their own terms apply to the payment, including refunds. The contract for the full version is concluded when the store confirms the purchase.</p>
  <p>3.3 The purchase belongs to your App Store or Google Play account, not to your game account. You can restore it on any phone signed in to the same store account. Deleting your game account does not remove it.</p>
  <p>3.4 You ask for a refund, including under the 14-day right of withdrawal that consumers in the EU, the EEA and the United Kingdom have, from the store that took the payment. We have no access to those payments and cannot refund them ourselves. If the store refuses a refund that you believe the law entitles you to, write to us. We reply within 14 days and help you with the store.</p>
  <p>3.5 The full version must conform to the contract, and you have the rights that chapter 5b of the Polish Consumer Rights Act gives a consumer for digital content. If it doesn't work as described, report it under section 6. We bring it into conformity free of charge within a reasonable time. If that isn't possible or doesn't work, you may ask for a price reduction or withdraw from the contract. The price is returned through Apple or Google, and we help you with that request. These terms don't limit those rights.</p>

  <h2 id="account">4. Account and contract</h2>
  <p>4.1 The game is for players aged 13 and over. If you are under 18, you need the consent of a parent or legal guardian where the law of your country requires it.</p>
  <p>4.2 You open an account by signing in with Apple or Google. The contract for the account is concluded at that first sign-in and runs for an indefinite term, until one of us ends it under section 7.</p>
  <p>4.3 Your account is personal. You may not sell it or hand it over to someone else.</p>

  <h2 id="nicknames">5. Nicknames and fair play</h2>
  <p>5.1 Your nickname is public. Anyone who opens the leaderboard sees it next to your scores. It must not be:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>offensive, vulgar, sexual or hateful, or an insult aimed at anyone</li>
    <li>the name of a real person you are not, or a name that pretends to be us</li>
    <li>someone's private information, such as a phone number or an address</li>
    <li>an advertisement or a link</li>
  </ul>
  <p>5.2 A word filter refuses some nicknames when you pick them. It does not catch everything, and passing it does not make a nickname acceptable.</p>
  <p>5.3 If your nickname breaks clause 5.1, we replace it with a neutral one, such as "Cook 12345". The new name shows at once next to all your scores. The game tells you which nickname we replaced, that it broke these rules, and how to appeal under clause 5.4. You can then pick another nickname straight away, without the usual 30-day wait. If you pick offensive nicknames again or the breach is serious, we may delete your account under clause 7.2.</p>
  <p>5.4 Anyone can report a nickname they find offensive or illegal by email to <a href="mailto:contact@arturwitkowski.com">contact@arturwitkowski.com</a>, with the nickname and the date of the leaderboard it appeared on. A person reads every report. If you think we renamed your nickname by mistake, write to us. We review the decision and answer within 14 days.</p>
  <p>5.5 You may not send contest scores that you did not get by playing the game, change the game or its traffic to get a better score, use bots or scripts against our server, or try to reach accounts or data that aren't yours. The server checks every score by replaying your moves and refuses one that does not match. If we find that you cheated, we may remove your results or delete your account.</p>

  <h2 id="complaints">6. Complaints</h2>
  <p>6.1 You can complain about the game, the full version or how we provide them by emailing <a href="mailto:contact@arturwitkowski.com">contact@arturwitkowski.com</a>. Describe the problem and what you want us to do, and give your nickname if it concerns your account.</p>
  <p>6.2 We answer complaints by email within 14 days of receiving them.</p>

  <h2 id="ending">7. Ending the contract</h2>
  <p>7.1 You can end the contract at any time, without giving a reason and at no cost, by deleting your account. In the game open Settings, then Account, and tap Delete account. If you no longer have the game, follow <a href="/midnight-pantry/privacy/#delete-account">section 11 of the privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p>7.2 We may delete your account with immediate effect if you seriously or repeatedly break these terms or the law.</p>
  <p>7.3 We may stop running the daily contest and the account features, but only after announcing it on this page and in the game's update notes in the App Store and on Google Play at least 30 days in advance. The game and the full version keep working offline on your phone.</p>

  <h2 id="liability">8. Availability and liability</h2>
  <p>8.1 We provide the free part of the game and the online features as they are. We don't guarantee that the server is always available or that the game is free of errors. We may pause the online features for maintenance or security and change the game, but we won't take away what the full version includes after you paid for it.</p>
  <p>8.2 The game, including its code, art, music, name and logo, belongs to us or our licensors. You may use it only to play.</p>
  <p>8.3 Nothing in these terms excludes or limits our liability for harm caused intentionally or through gross negligence, for personal injury, or any liability or right that mandatory consumer law protects.</p>

  <h2 id="stores">9. The app stores</h2>
  <p>9.1 On iPhone you get the game from Apple's App Store. Apple's standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement governs your licence to install and use it. These terms govern the rest. Apple is not a party to these terms and has no duty to maintain or support the game. If that agreement conflicts with mandatory consumer law, the law prevails.</p>
  <p>9.2 On Android you get the game from Google Play, and Google Play's terms govern your licence to install it.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">10. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>10.1 We may change these terms only because of a change in the law or a decision of a court or authority, new or changed features in the game, the security of the game or its players, or to prevent abuse.</p>
  <p>10.2 At least 14 days before a change applies, we publish the new text on this page and describe the change in the game's update notes in the App Store and on Google Play. If you don't accept the change, you can delete your account before it applies, at no cost. A change never reduces what the full version includes after you paid for it.</p>

  <h2 id="law">11. Law and disputes</h2>
  <p>11.1 Polish law governs these terms. If you are a consumer living in another country, you keep the protection of the mandatory rules of that country's law, and you may bring a claim in the courts of the country where you live.</p>
  <p>11.2 Consumers in Poland can get free help from a municipal or district consumer ombudsman (rzecznik konsumentów) or the Trade Inspection (Inspekcja Handlowa). Consumers in other EU countries can get help from the European Consumer Centre in their country.</p>
  <p>11.3 If any clause of these terms is found invalid, the other clauses remain in force.</p>

